  "notes": "Psychedelic synth-pop with heavily processed vocals. ⚠ `confidence` is low, and the research says why: it rates the entry medium-low and states that \"genre labels, multi-instrumentalism and the synth-pop turn [are] documented; rhythmic and harmonic detail inferred\". Three claims are actually researched and they carry the model. First, the pulse: \"backbeat on 2&4 straight with a motorik 8th-note drive\" and \"a dry, tight programmed-or-played kit with a plain backbeat and a repetitive 8th-note pulse; percussion is deliberately unobtrusive so the synth and vocal treatments carry the identity\" — so the kick is an unvarying 8th-note engine at near-zero syncopation, the snare is dry and short, `hihat.base` is 8th with the roll vocabulary off, and the perc lanes sit at the quietest gain in this batch. Second, the bass is the riff: \"a prominent, melodic analogue-style synth bass playing a repeating 8th-note figure that functions as the main riff\", which is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.32 with the bass register reaching high enough to read as a line rather than a floor; there is no `bass808` block because the entry says \"no 808\". Third, harmony: \"modal minor and major with drone-based harmony and chromatic pad movement\" over \"2- or 4-bar loops\", so `maxChords` is 3, `harmonicRhythm` is vamp-led and `susOrDimProb` carries the chromatic pad motion. Melody encodes \"narrow-range, mid-register and doubled with pitch/formant processing\" as a small `motifPitchCount` over a tight register with a `octave_echo` counter for the doubling. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic weights, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 115 (the midpoint of the stated 100—130 band); the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the buried-tenor claim is repeated here.",
